                <pb facs="0403" n="269" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg269"/>

                <head>No. 183.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-03-19"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 19, 1888</date>.
                        (Received May 5.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 591.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that the
                    Tsung-li Yamên has agreed that arrangements will be made to relieve the
                    foreigners from the present unsatisfactory system of “drawbacks” on the Yangtze.
                    The exact changes to be made have not been determined.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles
                        Denby.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
